DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't bet on a peace deal that isn't signed.</b> Oil fell 7% on hopes alone, and it has reversed on 'false dawns' before; keep your plan and don't trade on one Iran headline.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Fear & Greed is at 22.7 (Extreme Fear) and chips fell 12% in three days; regular buying (DCA) in broad funds beats guessing the bottom.",
"<b>Spread your risk beyond tech.</b> The Dow and 7 of 11 S&P sectors rose Monday while the Nasdaq fell; a broad or equal-weight fund keeps you from leaning too hard on AI.",
"<b>Expect swings this week.</b> The midterms today, AMD tonight and the jobs report Friday can all move prices.",
"<b>Rates are still high.</b> A December hike is about 72% likely; avoid new high-interest debt and lock in fixed rates where you can. Cash and short-term bonds still pay while you wait.",
"<b>Fuel may ease, but don't count on it.</b> WTI is near $96 and US diesel about $6.29; budget for prices bouncing back if talks fail.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a bet.</b> It bounced 1.8% to about $3,957; if you hold some, keep it a small slice.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC slipped to about $76.7k and about $6B has left Binance since withdrawals reopened; don't keep more on an exchange than you need.",
"<b>Thai investors: be patient and selective.</b> The SET (1,507.20) sits just above 1,500 support even as foreigners bought for a second day. In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, AP, TVO and PTT trade at or below their buy zones (green); check earnings and payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 22.7 = Extreme Fear, down from 26.2 on Friday and 29.8 a week ago. Momentum, options, volatility and safe-haven demand are all in extreme fear."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~44 = Elevated, down 2: Iran's president says he can seek a deal and Trump said 'No' to post-midterm strikes, but Russia's strikes intensified after the Kherson truce and no Iran deal is signed."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 13.2 = extreme fear: the index is below its 100-day average after another down day."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 34.0 = fear (82 NYSE highs vs 96 lows Monday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 40.8 = fear, a little better: most sectors rose Monday while tech fell."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 20.4 = extreme fear: lots of protection buying."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 12.5 = extreme fear: the VIX rose about 9% to about 21.2."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 1.8 = extreme fear: bonds keep beating stocks as money hides from tech."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 36.4 = fear, down from 43: lenders are getting more careful as Big Tech floods the bond market."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 62 (down from 67): Iran's president says he has authority to seek a deal and Trump said 'No' to strikes after the midterms, but nothing is signed. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 40 (up from 38), the biggest weight: fighting resumed in Kherson, a strike killed at least 26 at an aid center and 10 regions lost power, while talks in Abu Dhabi are expected."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 70 (down from 75): oil's 7% drop shows less escalation priced in, but Hormuz is still effectively shut and tanker and Houthi attacks remain a risk."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 18 (down from 20): Qatari mediators flew to Tehran and messages are moving between Iran and the US."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 25 (unchanged): no explicit nuclear threats; Iran's plan would restart talks on its nuclear program."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,541 Monday (−0.51%) after giving up a 1.1% morning gain as tech sold off again."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. +0.41% Monday, helped by cheaper oil and less tech exposure."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −1.07% Monday; the chip index is down 12% in three days and the Nasdaq 100 is in a correction."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.89% Monday: lower as falling oil eased inflation fears."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$96.5 (−7.4%) Monday, its biggest one-day drop since July, on hopes for an Iran deal."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$104.8 (−7.6%) Monday on Iran peace hopes; Hormuz is still effectively shut."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.29/gal (AAA, 3 Nov), just under the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,957 (+1.8%) Monday as lower oil eased Fed-hike worries; $4,000 is the line to beat."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$76.7k = bearish: Monday's bounce faded with tech, and about $6B has left Binance since withdrawals reopened."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct with two officials wanting a hike; next decision 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal; the Fed's preferred PCE gauge was 3.6% in September."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 72% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec as of 2 Nov."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. About 101.8, a little weaker Monday."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~157.9 = a weak yen; the BOJ held at 1.25% on Friday but said its 2% inflation goal is met, which points to more hikes."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT raised its 2026 growth forecast to 2.4%, sees inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,507.20 Mon 2 Nov (−0.75%), its intraday low was 1,506.54; brokers see support at 1,500 and resistance at 1,515."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿995M on 2 Nov, a second straight day of buying; October was about −฿6.6B (our sums of SET data)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
